I'd better keep going.

263
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:32,132
Great.

264
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:33,133
Okay. Monica.

265
00:10:33,174 --> 00:10:34,551
Yeah?

266
00:10:34,593 --> 00:10:35,469
Will you come here
with me for a minute?

267
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:37,178
Sure.

268
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:40,056
Are you wearing
waterproof mascara?

269
00:10:40,098 --> 00:10:40,932
No.

270
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:43,184
Oh, you're so screwed.

271
00:10:48,315 --> 00:10:49,274
Hey.

272
00:10:49,316 --> 00:10:51,401
What was that all about?

273
00:10:51,443 --> 00:10:55,071
She's gonna say good-bye
to each of us individually.

274
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:56,490
Are you kidding?

275
00:10:56,531 --> 00:10:57,698
Oh, my God.

276
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:59,075
Yeah, I know.

277
00:10:59,117 --> 00:11:01,202
It's gonna be even
worse for you. God.

278
00:11:01,244 --> 00:11:04,372
Well, just get ready to
do some serious crying.

279
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:08,709
Oh, man, I'm not going
to be able to handle this.

280
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:13,714
Now I know how my students
feel at the end of each year.

281
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:18,677
And why they act out by giving
me such bad evaluations.

282
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:25,726
Okay. I'd better...

283
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:29,481
just say what it is
I'm gonna say.

284
00:11:32,275 --> 00:11:34,068
None of the amazing things

285
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:36,737
that have happened to me
in the last ten years

286
00:11:36,779 --> 00:11:39,616
would have happened
if it wasn't for you.

287
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,744
No one has been...

288
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,455
more like a sister to me.

289
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:48,749
I know what you mean.

290
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:50,502
You're like a sister
to me, too.

291
00:11:54,088 --> 00:11:55,965
( sniffling )

292
00:11:56,007 --> 00:11:59,802
( choked up ):
I don't know what I'm
going to do without you.

293
00:12:01,054 --> 00:12:04,182
( indecipherable )

294
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:08,186
( indecipherable )

295
00:12:09,604 --> 00:12:11,856
What?

296
00:12:11,898 --> 00:12:15,694
I... said... I...

297
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:18,279
( indecipherable )

298
00:12:18,321 --> 00:12:20,323
That is so sweet.

299
00:12:27,372 --> 00:12:29,666
Oh, no, she took down Monica.

300
00:12:31,084 --> 00:12:33,712
And I'm the cryer in the family.

301
00:12:35,505 --> 00:12:37,215
ROSS:
Oh, God,
I could be next.

302
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:38,717
Maybe she won't talk to me

303
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:40,510
if it looks like we're deep
in conversation.

304
00:12:40,552 --> 00:12:41,844
Okay.

305
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:44,097
Oh, so that thing
you said about that thing,

306
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:46,140
it really made me think
about that other thing.

307
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,475
Uh, Rach...
Yeah?

308
00:12:47,517 --> 00:12:49,018
It's okay.
Chandler's talking to her.

309
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:51,563
Really made you think
about that thing, huh?

310
00:12:55,774 --> 00:12:57,694
Uh, Rach,
I think I have something

311
00:12:57,736 --> 00:13:01,114
that belongs to you.

312
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:06,411
Oh, I'm sure going
to miss pretending

313
00:13:06,453 --> 00:13:09,581
to laugh at your weird jokes
that I don't get.

314
00:13:09,623 --> 00:13:13,334
No, no.
They're really yours.

315
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:14,877
We found them
in your old room.

316
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,087
Well, these aren't mine.

317
00:13:16,129 --> 00:13:17,422
Maybe Monica used
to use them with...

318
00:13:17,464 --> 00:13:19,215
Don't say Richard.

319
00:13:20,467 --> 00:13:23,511
Well, if they're not Monica's
and they're not yours,

320
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:24,512
then whose are they?

321
00:13:24,554 --> 00:13:25,888
I think
you're forgetting

322
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,932
the kinkiest
former resident
of that room.

323
00:13:27,974 --> 00:13:29,267
Pheebs!

324
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:31,810
Yeah?

325
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:34,606
I think these are yours.

326
00:13:34,648 --> 00:13:36,650
These are not mine.

327
00:13:36,691 --> 00:13:38,777
Look at how flimsy they are.

328
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,153
Come on.

329
00:13:42,489 --> 00:13:45,575
My God. You try to hang a guy
from a water pipe with these,

330
00:13:45,617 --> 00:13:49,287
they'll snap
like a piece of licorice.

331
00:13:49,329 --> 00:13:50,955
Can I talk to you
alone for a minute?

332
00:13:50,997 --> 00:13:52,290
Sure.

333
00:13:55,335 --> 00:13:57,462
You don't really
handcuff guys

334
00:13:57,504 --> 00:13:59,213
to water pipes, do you?

335
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:01,299
Where do you think
Mike really is?

336
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:12,851
Oh, honey...

337
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:14,228
Let me just say something.

338
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:15,522
Because once we get
into this,

339
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:17,023
I'm going to get
all uncomfortable

340
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:19,693
and probably make
some stupid joke.

341
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:24,656
I just want to say
that I... I love you...

342
00:14:24,698 --> 00:14:29,494
and I'm going
to miss you.

343
00:14:29,536 --> 00:14:32,539
And I'm so sad
that you're leaving.

344
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:38,670
Oh, you know what?

345
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:40,839
Let's not say anything else.

346
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,382
I love you.

347
00:14:44,217 --> 00:14:45,343
Not so tight.

348
00:14:45,385 --> 00:14:46,093
( blows raspberry )

349
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:47,303
Oh!

350
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:49,930
Chandler...

351
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:51,641
I'm sorry.
Just give me
one more chance.

352
00:14:51,683 --> 00:14:52,642
Okay.
Okay.

353
00:14:52,684 --> 00:14:53,976
Oh...

354
00:14:54,018 --> 00:14:55,144
( blows raspberry )

355
00:14:55,186 --> 00:14:56,521
Oh!
I'm sorry.

356
00:14:56,563 --> 00:14:57,856
Just go. Just go.

357
00:14:57,938 --> 00:14:59,232
I can't. I can't.

358
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:06,447
So I guess you're next.

359
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:07,448
You ready?

360
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:08,491
I don't think so.

361
00:15:08,533 --> 00:15:10,076
Oh, you're
definitely not.

362
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:12,161
I haven't cried
like that in years.

363
00:15:12,203 --> 00:15:14,622
You cried yesterday
at the 6:00 news.

364
00:15:14,664 --> 00:15:18,167
That old woman was being scammed
by her mechanic.

365
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:23,172
God, I can't believe
she saved me for last.

366
00:15:23,214 --> 00:15:24,674
Why are they taking so long?

367
00:15:24,716 --> 00:15:26,925
I don't know,
but, God, Joey seems

368
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:29,387
to be handling it
surprisingly well.

369
00:15:32,766 --> 00:15:34,183
ALL:
No! No, wait!

370
00:15:42,734 --> 00:15:45,361
Okay, here we go.

371
00:15:45,403 --> 00:15:47,363
( sighs )

372
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:49,449
Well.

373
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,284
Yeah.

374
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:54,746
I think I'm going
to take off.

375
00:15:57,415 --> 00:15:59,166
Huh?

376
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:01,669
Oh, you guys, this was
an amazing night.

377
00:16:01,711 --> 00:16:03,170
Thank you so much.

378
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:04,672
I love you.

379
00:16:04,714 --> 00:16:06,591
Good night.

380
00:16:06,633 --> 00:16:08,676
( door opens )

381
00:16:08,718 --> 00:16:10,052
( door shuts )

382
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:12,472
What?!

383
00:16:15,558 --> 00:16:17,852
I don't get a good-bye?!

384
00:16:17,894 --> 00:16:19,938
Lucky bastard.

385
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:28,696
Unbelievable.

386
00:16:28,738 --> 00:16:30,949
She says good-bye
to everyone but me.

387
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:33,576
Well, maybe she thought that
with all of your history,

388
00:16:33,618 --> 00:16:35,995
it could be,
you know, implicit.

389
00:16:36,036 --> 00:16:39,707
Well, it needs to be plicit!

390
00:16:39,749 --> 00:16:41,167
Let's think about this.

391
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:43,169
I mean, there's got
to be an explanation.

392
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:45,129
Did you do anything
to make her mad?

393
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:46,881
No, I don't think so.

394
00:16:46,923 --> 00:16:50,384
You know, maybe she was just
really spent from our talk.

395
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:51,845
It was pretty intense.

396
00:16:51,886 --> 00:16:52,929
Yeah, mine, too.

397
00:16:52,971 --> 00:16:54,012
Mine was a humdinger.

398
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:54,931
Okay!

399
00:16:56,516 --> 00:16:58,518
I mean,
don't I deserve anything?

400
00:16:58,559 --> 00:17:02,021
I mean, a... a few tears,
a... a cursory hug?

401
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,108
Not from you!

402
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:10,530
Ross, if you're this upset,
you should go and talk to her.

403
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:11,531
And say what?

404
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:13,240
"You owe me a good-bye"?

405
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:15,284
He's got more pride
than that.

406
00:17:15,326 --> 00:17:16,744
The hell I do!

407
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:22,291
I don't get a good-bye?!

408
00:17:22,333 --> 00:17:23,543
What?

409
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:25,628
Everyone gets
a good-bye but me?

410
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:27,881
What do I got to do
to get a good-bye, huh?

411
00:17:27,922 --> 00:17:29,716
Uh, be best friends with you?

412
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:31,050
Uh, go out with you?

413
00:17:31,091 --> 00:17:32,385
Have-have a baby with you?

414
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:33,386
Oh, wait a minute!
Wait a minute!

415
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:35,053
I did all those things!

416
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:37,223
Ross, I...
Or maybe...

417
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:39,559
Maybe I'm just
not giving you
enough credit.

418
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:43,145
Uh, I mean, it is difficult
to say good-bye to fivepeople.

419
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:45,398
Uh, "Good-bye. Good-bye,
Good-bye. Good-bye.

420
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:46,399
( choking up ):
Goo..."

421
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,359
It's physically impossible!

422
00:17:50,862 --> 00:17:55,073
You know what, after all we've
been through, I can't believe

423
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:57,535
this is how you want
to leave things between us.

424
00:17:57,577 --> 00:17:59,787
Have a... have a good time
in Paris.

425
00:18:04,709 --> 00:18:06,711
I hope Ross
isn't too upset.

426
00:18:06,753 --> 00:18:09,296
I'm sure he's not
more bummed out
than I am.

427
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:10,297
Tell me about it.

428
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:11,632
Well, you can't say

429
00:18:11,674 --> 00:18:13,927
we don't know how
to throw a party.

430
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:16,345
All right, I think
I'm going to head out.

431
00:18:16,387 --> 00:18:19,098
Uh, where do you think
you're going?

432
00:18:19,139 --> 00:18:21,851
I thought I was going home
to go to bed, but I'm sensing

433
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:24,311
there's something less fun
for me to do here.

434
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:26,773
Well, we're moving
in a couple of days,

435
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,232
and we got a lot
of packing to do.

436
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:30,192
It'd be great if you guys
could pitch in.

437
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:32,486
Joey and I can finish up
in the guest room.

438
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:35,573
Oh, yeah, yeah. Good idea.

439
00:18:35,615 --> 00:18:36,908
Oh, no.

440
00:18:36,950 --> 00:18:38,158
You and Phoebe are going
to help me in here.

441
00:18:39,452 --> 00:18:41,203
You couldn't be cool.

442
00:18:43,456 --> 00:18:45,207
Okay, we're going to
start in the kitchen.

443
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:46,751
Plates get put
into plate protectors

444
00:18:46,793 --> 00:18:48,168
and get stacked ten to a box.

445
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,796
The silverware gets bundled
in rubber bands

446
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:51,798
and then bubble-wrapped.
Got it?

447
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:53,424
Yeah.
Yeah.
Good.

448
00:18:53,466 --> 00:18:55,051
Now I need you
to be careful
and efficient.

449
00:18:55,093 --> 00:18:56,844
And remember,
if I am harsh with you,

450
00:18:56,886 --> 00:18:59,764
it's only because
you're doing it wrong.

451
00:19:01,641 --> 00:19:04,894
Hey, Mon, I think I figured out
whose handcuffs they are.

452
00:19:04,936 --> 00:19:06,145
You did? How?

453
00:19:06,186 --> 00:19:07,772
Well, I was cleaning
out the closet

454
00:19:07,814 --> 00:19:11,985
and I found some pictures
of them... being used.

455
00:19:12,026 --> 00:19:13,486
Oh, my God.
Let me see.

456
00:19:15,029 --> 00:19:16,155
( gasps )

457
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:17,531
Who's that dirty old lady?

458
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:20,534
Monica's grandmother.

459
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:25,372
God, Nana liked it rough!

460
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:28,042
Hi.

461
00:19:28,084 --> 00:19:29,669
Hey.
Hey.

462
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:30,670
Here, have a seat.
Have a seat.

463
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:31,796
How was your night?

464
00:19:31,838 --> 00:19:33,172
Oh, it was okay.
I went to a movie

465
00:19:33,213 --> 00:19:35,299
with my cousin
and then out for dinner.

466
00:19:35,341 --> 00:19:37,927
We went to this place
that had...

467
00:19:37,969 --> 00:19:39,012
Ooh!

468
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:42,348
Ooh.

469
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:43,933
( sighs )

470
00:19:43,975 --> 00:19:47,061
Anyway, they had these really
amazing cheeseburgers.

471
00:19:49,022 --> 00:19:51,858
Erica, are you okay?

472
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:53,400
Yeah. You know,
maybe I ate too much.

473
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:55,402
I keep getting
these stomachaches.

474
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:57,989
The come and go like
every few minutes.

475
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:00,825
Oh, my God!

476
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:04,537
Relax, we'll just get her
some antacids.

477
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:06,164
She doesn't have a stomachache!

478
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,206
She's in labor!

479
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:08,374
On, my God!

480
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:09,792
Yeah, you got to get
to the hospital!

481
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:11,169
Okay, Chandler,
get the coats!

482
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,378
Erica, let's go!

483
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:14,254
Phoebe and Joey,
keep packing!

484
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:15,798
Oh, my God, we're going...

485
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:18,509
We're going
to have a baby!

486
00:20:18,551 --> 00:20:19,552
Oh, my God!

487
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:21,261
We're going to have a baby!

488
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:23,139
Oh, God, I've got to sit down!

489
00:20:23,181 --> 00:20:25,516
I got to sit down. Oh!

490
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:26,726
( labored breathing )

491
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:27,852
Honey, it's going
to be okay.

492
00:20:27,894 --> 00:20:30,146
You can do this! Just breathe.

493
00:20:30,188 --> 00:20:33,149
Okay, okay.

494
00:20:33,191 --> 00:20:34,942
Okay, I feel...
I feel a little better.

495
00:20:34,984 --> 00:20:36,652
Oh!

496
00:20:36,694 --> 00:20:38,071
Are you sure?

497
00:20:38,112 --> 00:20:40,156
Oh, yes, I'm sure.

498
00:20:40,198 --> 00:20:41,490
Oh, honey, let's go.

499
00:20:41,532 --> 00:20:42,408
Okay.
Come on.

500
00:20:42,449 --> 00:20:43,617
Okay, bye,
everyone!

501
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:45,411
Bye-bye. We're having a baby!

502
00:20:45,452 --> 00:20:46,662
Chandler, wait, wait, wait!

503
00:20:46,704 --> 00:20:47,788
What?

504
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,123
If you get a second,

505
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:50,499
find out where
she got that cheeseburger.

506
00:20:57,715 --> 00:20:59,175
( door slams )

507
00:20:59,217 --> 00:21:00,760
You really think
I didn't say good-bye to you

508
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:02,011
because I don't care?

509
00:21:02,053 --> 00:21:03,721
That's what it seemed like.

510
00:21:03,763 --> 00:21:06,224
I cannot believe
that after ten years,

511
00:21:06,264 --> 00:21:08,601
you do not know
one thing about me.

512
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:10,561
Fine. Then why didn't you
say something?

513
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:14,065
Because it is too damn hard,
Ross.

514
00:21:14,107 --> 00:21:16,901
I can't even begin
to explain to you

515
00:21:16,943 --> 00:21:18,819
how much I am going
to miss you.

516
00:21:18,861 --> 00:21:20,947
When I think about
not seeing you

517
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:23,657
every day, it makes
me not want to go,

518
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:24,658
okay?

519
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,994
So if you think
that, that

520
00:21:27,036 --> 00:21:28,621
I didn't say good-bye to you

521
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:30,456
because you don't mean as much
to me as everybody else,

522
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:31,999
you're wrong.

523
00:21:32,041 --> 00:21:34,794
It's because
you mean more to me.

524
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:35,920
So there, all right?!

525
00:21:35,962 --> 00:21:37,088
There's your good-bye!

